WEBVTT

00:00:01.484 --> 00:00:03.460
SIEM stands for Security Information and Event Management.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.300
The information component focuses on collecting, storing,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.315
and managing logs and security data.

00:00:08.315 --> 00:00:12.030
The event management component focuses on identifying meaningful activity through

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.010
searches,

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.744
correlations, alerts, and investigations.

00:00:14.744 --> 00:00:19.075
SIEM platforms combine these functions to help security teams transform raw data into

00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:20.780
operational awareness.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.980
Instead of looking at individual systems separately,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.831
analysts can investigate activity across the environment from a centralized interface.

00:00:26.831 --> 00:00:30.860
A SIEM is best understood as an operational capability, not a magic product.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.300
It is useful when the right data is collected, normalized, searched, correlated, tuned,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.410
and reviewed by people who understand the environment.
